# openjdk-bin is NOT a second JDK by accident -- it is what breaks the bootstrap
# cycle. dev-java/openjdk[system-bootstrap] (on by default, and REQUIRED_USE
# "!system-bootstrap? ( ppc64 )" makes turning it off impossible on amd64)
# depends on
#     || ( dev-java/openjdk-bin:${SLOT}  dev-java/openjdk:${SLOT} )
# and with only the source ebuild in the plan Portage satisfies that branch with
# openjdk ITSELF, which step12-kde-resolve reported as
#     Error: circular dependencies: openjdk-25 depends on openjdk-25 (buildtime)
# Listing the binary makes the first branch reachable (lab, 2026-09-12).
dev-java/openjdk-bin
